To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 9,009 and 14,014, I'll start by breaking down both numbers into their prime factors. 

First, let's factorize 9,009. I know that 9 times 1,001 is 9,009. Now, I'll factorize 1,001 further. 1,001 can be factored into 7 times 143, and 143 is 11 times 13. So, the prime factors of 9,009 are 3, 7, 11, and 13.

Next, I'll factorize 14,014. I notice that it's even, so it's divisible by 2. Dividing 14,014 by 2 gives 7,007. Now, I'll factorize 7,007. Adding the digits of 7,007 gives me 14, which is not divisible by 3, so 3 is not a factor. Checking divisibility by 7, 7,007 divided by 7 equals 1,001. From earlier, I know 1,001 is 7 times 11 times 13. Therefore, the prime factors of 14,014 are 2, 7, 11, and 13.

Finally, I'll compare the prime factors of both numbers and identify the common ones. Both have 7, 11, and 13 as common prime factors. Multiplying these together gives the GCD: 7 times 11 is 77, and 77 times 13 is 1,001. So, the greatest common divisor of 9,009 and 14,014 is 1,001.

